I come out of the market.
Suddenly, the sky becomes very dark.
Today, the weather is changing very fast.
Heavy rain starts again.
I quickly open my umbrella.
But this rain is very heavy.
There is a large building ahead.
That is a museum.
I hurriedly go in through the gates of that museum.
I run towards the large roof of the entrance.
I take shelter from the rain there.
I close my umbrella.
I firmly shake the water off the umbrella.
Five months ago, in January, the weather was very different.
There was no rain at all in Mumbai then.
But this monsoon is entirely different.
I look once at those dark clouds outside.
And then I step inside the museum.
